// layer L13
// 20 input-sanitization taint demo: lines from stdin carry taint(#user), and
// the page written to stdout demands taint(#clean). Interpolation is `++`, so
// taint flows through it; the commented line is the compile error (taint(#user)
// reaches a taint(#clean) sink), and the line after it is the fix: `sanitize`
// is the only edge that lowers the taint. variants/20-taint-error.zed is the
// program with the error left in. This corpus assumes sanitize HTML-escapes
// the five characters & < > " ' (the library fixes its text at step L13.2).
main(stdin: Lines with taint(#user)) -> (stdout: Lines with taint(#clean)) {
  // stdout <- stdin.map(l -> "<li>${l}</li>");             // ✗ taint(#user) reaches a taint(#clean) port
  stdout <- stdin.map(l -> "<li>${sanitize(l)}</li>");       // ✓
}
